Dictionaries-A dictionary in Python is a way to store information as key-value pairs.
Ex-student = {
    "name": "Kartik",
    "age": 20,
}
Here 
"name" is a key, and "Rahul" is its value
"age" is a key, and 20 is its value
Methods of dictionaries are -
1. keys()
Returns all the keys.
print(student.keys())
2. values()
Returns all the values.
print(student.values())
3. items()
Returns both keys and values.
